[SIZE=5][B]Introduction[/B][/SIZE]
Beelink stopped at Android 9 (last firmware 2022-04-01) and every community ROM for this box so far is a repackaged stock 9. This thread brings a current Android TV to the plain Beelink [B]GT-King[/B] (black, Amlogic S922X, 4 GB / 64 GB, board GTKing-D4X16 rev 2.0–4.0). Not for the GT-King Pro (different DTB, Wi-Fi module and remote table).

Two builds are available:
[LIST]
[*][B]v1[/B] — LineageOS 22.2 (Android 15 TV), 32-bit userspace (like the stock firmware), Google apps included.
[*][B]v3[/B] — Android 15 TV with a [B]64-bit[/B] userspace, based on voodik's LineageOS 22.1 ATV for the ODROID-N2 (same S922X SoC) with GT-King kernel, device tree and driver fixes. [B]Take v3 if you want emulation (PS2, GameCube/Wii).[/B] (v3 = the former v2 with the audio fix below; v2 is superseded and no longer offered.)
[/LIST]
Both keep the stock Beelink bootloader (its BL2 holds the LPDDR4 training) and chain-load a LineageOS u-boot from a separate partition, so the box can always go back to stock.

[SIZE=5][B]What's new in v3 (2026-10-09)[/B][/SIZE]
Fixes [B]HDMI / S-PDIF / analog (3.5 mm) audio[/B], which was silent on v2 — only Bluetooth audio worked. The 64-bit device tree left the internal audio mux (TOHDMITX) pointing at the wrong source; v3 sets it so the mux follows the stream. v3 is otherwise identical to v2 — same kernel, system, vendor and bootloader, only the device-tree partition changed. [B]If you are on v2 and only get sound over Bluetooth, flash v3.[/B]

